<bounds x="1245" y="195" width="273" height="276"/>
<comment>Business Rule:
- A job&apos;s description defines employee access level in the system
- Every record in ORDERDETAILS must refer to a valid order and a valid product.
- The combination of OrderID and ProductID in ORDERDETAILS must be unique (i.e., a product cannot appear more than once per order).
- If the customer decides to cancel the order, the total amount and payment method will be null, but the status must be &apos;Canceled&apos; and cannot be null.
- Customer Name is not nullable because we need it to announce the customer regarding the status of the order.
- The OrderDetails table is used to list out the different products in the customer&apos;s order; if the customer decides to cancel the order, the orderdetails will not appear.</comment>
</OView>
